Failure Scenario 1: Health Check False Positive
Server responds:
HTTP 200 OK
but database is down.
Load balancer still routes traffic.
Users receive errors.
________________________________________
Real companies use:
Deep Health Checks
instead of simple heartbeat checks.
________________________________________
Failure Scenario 2: TLS Overload
Imagine:
500,000 new HTTPS connections/sec
TLS handshakes become bottleneck.
Solutions:
•	Hardware acceleration
•	TLS session reuse
•	Multiple load balancers
________________________________________
Failure Scenario 3: Metrics Failure
Traffic working.
Monitoring broken.
________________________________________
Engineers cannot see:
•	latency spikes
•	failures
•	overload
Very dangerous.
Many outages become worse because observability is missing.
