Performance Thinking
When Principal Engineers review a load balancer, they ask:
Which component becomes the bottleneck first?
Possible answers:
•	listener saturation
•	TLS CPU exhaustion
•	routing rule explosion
•	connection table size
•	health check delays
Not:
Which algorithm are we using?
Thinking about bottlenecks is what differentiates system design from memorization.
